##################################################
# Project Specific
##################################################

# A pattern with a slash in the middle (like the one below) is anchored to the
# directory containing this .gitignore -- it only matches ./ml/models/, not
# backend/ml/models/, where trained model artifacts actually land (see
# app/core/config.py Settings.ml_model_path). Both are listed explicitly rather than
# relying on one non-anchored pattern to cover both, so this stays correct if a
# repo-root ml/ directory is ever introduced alongside backend/'s.
ml/models/
backend/ml/models/
data/